<!--
  The Today widget, large: from 250 by 280dp on Android 12 and later (WidgetRenderer.TODAY_SIZES), the
  4 by 4 it is placed at by default. The SajdaTime mark with the date and the Hijri date; the countdown
  card (the next prayer, its time, the countdown and the day's five bars); then the six rows, weighted
  to fill. The countdown card uses the Next widget's ids, so one function fills both.

  Measured: the six rows fit at 250 by 280dp at the normal text size. From 130 percent text the large
  layout is not used, because the countdown card leaves room for only three rows (WidgetRenderer).

  The mark appears here and on the "set your location" state only, never on the small widgets
  (docs/plans/2026-10-widget-redesign/RESEARCH.md). No town name: a home screen is seen by others.

  Rules for every widget layout (WidgetResourcesTest fails the build on each): no android:text, because
  the launcher would resolve it in the PHONE's language; only classes a RemoteViews may inflate (no plain
  View, so hairlines and progress bars are ImageViews with a drawable); every text view hidden from
  TalkBack, the root carries one spoken sentence; every colour a resource, resolved by the launcher at
  each draw so the widget follows the phone's dark mode. Glyphs are drawn white and tinted here, for the
  same reason (lesson 130).

  The countdown is set in the light weight, Apple Clock style, and its size is written from
  WidgetRenderer in dp rather than sp: it is already about three times the body text, and scaled by a
  large font setting it pushed the prayer name off a 110dp widget. Names and times stay in sp.

  tools:ignore on the root, all three deliberate: the empty weighted LinearLayouts are the gaps that
  spread the content (HANDOVER lesson 142), the nested weight is the wide layout's two columns, and a
  compound drawable cannot be tinted per theme from a layout the way an ImageView's glyph is.
-->
<LinearLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingStart="10dp"
    android:paddingTop="12dp"
    android:paddingEnd="10dp"
    android:paddingBottom="8dp"
    tools:ignore="UselessLeaf,NestedWeights,UseCompoundDrawables">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_header"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="4dp"
        android:paddingEnd="4dp">
        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="28dp"
            android:layout_height="28dp"
            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
            android:src="@drawable/widget_mark" />
